Three chemicals in this proposed action– acrylonitrile, vinyl chloride and 4,4-methylene 
bis(2-chloroaniline) (also referred to as ‘bisamine’) – have the most direct relation to 
groundwater in their product use in: reverse osmosis to clean water, water distribution 
and contaminant containment, respectively. We would ask that these uses be taken into 
account in the risk assessment.
Thank you for the opportunity to comment on this proposed action.
