Performance. Because Benzenamine Is Present as an Impurity in Such Additives, 
It May Be Released Into the Air During Tire Manufacturing and May Remain in 
the Final Tire Product at Very Low Concentrations. Benzenamine May Also Be 
Released into the Air or Water During Tire Use at Very Low Concentrations.3  
It is unclear why this information was not incorporated into the prioritization screening 
review.  Moreover, it highlights the limitations of the CDR data for elucidating the detail 
regarding the use of any particular chemical.  ACC appreciates EPA’s acknowledgement of these 
limitations and other information limits when it states:  
Based on the information reported to, HPCDS, ChemExpo, studies found during 
EPA’s screening review and public comment, there is uncertainty regarding use 
of benzenamine in these categories of consumer products, EPA seeks 
confirmation, comment or additional information on consumer uses. EPA will 
consider public comments received regarding the presence of benzenamine in 
consumer products and articles.4 
It would be helpful if the prioritization screening reviews included readily available 
information about chemical uses.  The history of aniline (benzenamine) dyes is well known 
having been discovered and commercialized over 160 years ago.5,6  Many of those dyes are still 
used today and are likely to contain traces of aniline as impurities.  Consequently, the presence 
of aniline in dyed products, like textiles, is not surprising and is appropriate for inclusion in the 
prioritization screening review. 
III. 
Comments Related to Data for the Substances 
A. 
EPA Should Collect Available Occupational Exposure Limit (OEL) Data for Each 
Chemical and Provide Context Regarding Current Workplace Exposure Controls. 
ACC does not agree with the agency’s policy decision to include all occupational 
exposures in all risk evaluations all the time. However, assuming that the agency continues to 
expansively scope in all worker exposures under its revised risk evaluation framework rule, it 
can and should begin collecting available OEL data during the prioritization step.  OEL values 
 
